ion by sequence homology. This gene encodes a 39S subunit protein. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. Pseudogenes corresponding to this gene are found on chromosomes 6p and 12p. Read-through transcription also exists between this gene and the neighboring upstream lipoyltransferase 1 (LIPT1) gene. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[],"uniprot_source":null,"retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}